1
00:00:12,610 --> 00:00:16,270
WE COMMEMORATE ALPAY GÖLTEKİN, WHO
CONTRIBUTED TO OUR ANCESTORS'...

2
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:19,960
...HEROIC EPICS WITH HIS MUSIC AND
SHAPED THE FLOW OF HISTORY, WITH RESPECT.

3
00:00:33,631 --> 00:00:41,121
Please contact turkision@gmail.com
for any inquiries

4
00:02:10,486 --> 00:02:14,486
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

5
00:02:20,809 --> 00:02:21,539
Father.

6
00:02:30,876 --> 00:02:31,606
Father!

7
00:02:33,561 --> 00:02:34,311
Father!

8
00:02:36,118 --> 00:02:36,878
Father!

9
00:02:39,221 --> 00:02:40,061
Father!

10
00:02:41,949 --> 00:02:42,759
Father!

11
00:02:49,559 --> 00:02:52,059
I’m going to kill you with my bare
hands, Osman!

12
00:02:52,316 --> 00:02:54,886
Then I will feed the wolves and birds
with your flesh.

13
00:02:54,886 --> 00:02:56,366
My uncle is not dead, Bahadır.

14
00:03:10,175 --> 00:03:10,875
Father!

15
00:03:13,722 --> 00:03:15,182
Bahadır is here, Father.

16
00:03:42,278 --> 00:03:44,188
Bahadır is here.

17
00:03:45,942 --> 00:03:46,642
My son.

18
00:03:49,985 --> 00:03:50,725
Bahadır.

19
00:03:51,784 --> 00:03:52,724
How di-

20
00:03:52,724 --> 00:03:54,124
How did you find me?

21
00:03:55,017 --> 00:03:55,757
Aygül.

22
00:03:56,906 --> 00:03:57,916
Aygül, father!

23
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:10,100
She brought us here.

24
00:04:11,664 --> 00:04:13,104
Oh my Aygül.

25
00:04:15,794 --> 00:04:17,354
Oh my lioness daughter...

26
00:04:19,243 --> 00:04:20,803
...oh my heroic daughter.

27
00:04:24,363 --> 00:04:25,923
If my father was dead…

28
00:04:25,923 --> 00:04:29,393
...I would have burned you alive at
the middle of the Kayı tent, Osman!

29
00:04:29,565 --> 00:04:30,325
Bahadır!

30
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:34,647
Don’t forget that you will account for
what your mouth is capable of saying...

31
00:04:34,647 --> 00:04:36,967
...in this world, not afterlife!

32
00:04:43,661 --> 00:04:45,101
I don’t give accounts.

33
00:04:47,295 --> 00:04:49,025
I only accept them, Osman!

34
00:05:04,023 --> 00:05:04,813
Bahadır!

35
00:05:05,483 --> 00:05:06,393
My son!

36
00:05:28,758 --> 00:05:31,688
We successfully escorted Princess to the
place Osman wanted.

37
00:05:32,985 --> 00:05:35,885
Thanks to Allah, we fulfilled this duty
properly, my Brother.

38
00:05:36,662 --> 00:05:40,662
Now that we have found each other and we
are side by side...

39
00:05:41,541 --> 00:05:44,921
...we will win many battles together,
brother.

40
00:05:44,921 --> 00:05:46,601
Inshallah, brother.

41
00:05:49,162 --> 00:05:50,572
What are we going to do now?

42
00:05:50,572 --> 00:05:52,012
Are we going to Tent now?

43
00:05:52,012 --> 00:05:53,142
What happened?

44
00:05:53,142 --> 00:05:54,812
Do you miss the life style at Tent?

45
00:05:56,106 --> 00:05:57,686
You can’t imagine, brother.

46
00:05:57,686 --> 00:05:58,446
You can’t.

47
00:06:00,968 --> 00:06:02,778
Brother, we will leave for Tent now.

48
00:06:02,778 --> 00:06:04,878
You will go to Alişar’s mansion...

49
00:06:04,878 --> 00:06:06,568
...and keep your eyes open.

50
00:06:07,785 --> 00:06:10,935
You will inform us if something happens.

51
00:06:12,377 --> 00:06:14,817
For now, Tent is no good to you.

52
00:06:18,475 --> 00:06:20,445
As you wish my brother.

53
00:06:22,247 --> 00:06:24,697
I waited my whole life so I can wait more.

54
00:06:48,414 --> 00:06:49,114
Brother.

55
00:06:49,414 --> 00:06:50,544
May you be careful.

56
00:06:51,650 --> 00:06:53,230
We have lots of enemies.

57
00:06:53,325 --> 00:06:55,655
For the ones who have brothers like
Konur Alp...

58
00:06:55,655 --> 00:06:57,755
...even dragon-like enemies are nothing.

59
00:06:58,224 --> 00:07:00,164
Don’t worry about me brother.

60
00:07:00,164 --> 00:07:02,844
A soldier’s fate is never returning one
day.

61
00:07:02,844 --> 00:07:04,724
Tomorrow it is, if not today.

62
00:07:05,886 --> 00:07:07,876
May you give your blessing to me.

63
00:07:32,973 --> 00:07:34,953
Alps! Let’s go!

64
00:07:41,499 --> 00:07:42,799
You will die, Osman!

65
00:07:44,060 --> 00:07:45,160
I will kill you!

66
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:45,860
Enough!

67
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:50,995
I need Osman alive.

68
00:07:51,824 --> 00:07:53,784
Try not to cross your line, Böke.

69
00:07:53,784 --> 00:07:56,014
He is the one who killed my brother.

70
00:07:57,036 --> 00:07:58,836
His blood is halal only to us.

71
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:04,690
Hold you horses down, you crazy boy!

72
00:08:08,441 --> 00:08:12,211
Or else I will kill you before Osman does.

73
00:08:18,275 --> 00:08:19,565
Commander Böke!

74
00:08:19,879 --> 00:08:21,149
Commander Böke!

75
00:08:22,551 --> 00:08:23,771
This is our matter.

76
00:08:24,245 --> 00:08:26,805
Osman is going to die!

77
00:08:28,668 --> 00:08:32,248
Every matter corcens Geyhatu first…

78
00:08:33,383 --> 00:08:35,693
…then me at this Border, Dündar Bey.

79
00:08:37,784 --> 00:08:40,054
I see everyone is obsessed with me.

80
00:08:43,454 --> 00:08:45,804
I am strong enough to fight all of
you.

81
00:08:54,299 --> 00:08:57,269
So you can tell this to mighty Geyhatu
yourself, Osman.

82
00:08:58,938 --> 00:09:00,198
I feel sorry for you.

83
00:09:01,475 --> 00:09:05,095
He is more cruel than he is forgiving.

84
00:09:06,478 --> 00:09:09,448
Unlike you, we neither walk around with a
leash on our neck...

85
00:09:10,403 --> 00:09:12,723
…nor do we sell our soul to nobody.

86
00:09:16,580 --> 00:09:18,330
Most importantly...

87
00:09:18,710 --> 00:09:21,240
...we know no greater power than Allah.

88
00:09:25,967 --> 00:09:29,967
How dare you try to stick your nose into a
matter of our Tent?

89
00:09:30,617 --> 00:09:32,627
Osman killed my son!

90
00:09:32,627 --> 00:09:34,157
Don’t you understand?

91
00:09:41,486 --> 00:09:42,866
If you touch him...

92
00:09:44,276 --> 00:09:46,456
...I will kill your only remaining son.

93
00:09:47,686 --> 00:09:50,396
And, I will feed you with his corpse
until you puke.

94
00:09:54,255 --> 00:09:55,215
Dündar Bey!

95
00:09:56,446 --> 00:09:57,746
Commander Böke!

96
00:09:59,034 --> 00:10:00,224
Enough already.

97
00:10:04,615 --> 00:10:05,935
You see that Boran?

98
00:10:07,050 --> 00:10:09,380
We are feasts for jackals around here.

99
00:10:10,171 --> 00:10:12,291
They threaten each other over food.

100
00:10:15,254 --> 00:10:16,264
Tie them now!

101
00:11:10,218 --> 00:11:14,008
I will hold a feast every year on the
day you die, Osman!

102
00:11:18,423 --> 00:11:21,253
Now that the biggest danger is tied…

103
00:11:23,207 --> 00:11:25,057
…your absolute end is here, Osman.

104
00:11:25,792 --> 00:11:26,562
It’s here.

105
00:12:41,650 --> 00:12:42,930
Zöhre Hatun!

106
00:13:01,896 --> 00:13:03,856
Don't do it, Zöhre Hatun!

107
00:13:03,856 --> 00:13:06,296
I don’t want to hurt you.

108
00:13:07,238 --> 00:13:10,568
If your Bey and children learn that you
got shot while running away...

109
00:13:11,244 --> 00:13:12,864
...they will become sad.

110
00:13:13,871 --> 00:13:15,441
Come with me and know your place.

111
00:13:15,441 --> 00:13:21,791
In the future, I am going to make all of
you pay for days like today.

112
00:13:23,911 --> 00:13:25,491
I will come with you...

113
00:13:26,232 --> 00:13:30,122
…but don’t you forget about what I just
said.

114
00:13:38,983 --> 00:13:42,283
As long as he lives, none of us...

115
00:13:42,283 --> 00:13:44,333
…not even Geyhatu...

116
00:13:44,333 --> 00:13:45,393
...can find peace.

117
00:13:49,332 --> 00:13:52,362
What on earth do you have on your
mind?

118
00:13:52,362 --> 00:13:53,712
Commander Böke?

119
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:58,143
I said his blood is halal to me!

120
00:13:58,143 --> 00:13:59,313
Can’t you hear?

121
00:13:59,313 --> 00:14:00,353
Enough!

122
00:14:00,433 --> 00:14:01,353
Enough it is!

123
00:14:01,353 --> 00:14:02,353
My Bey...

124
00:14:02,353 --> 00:14:04,543
...these dogs have no intention of
killing us.

125
00:14:04,543 --> 00:14:07,023
It’s obvious Geyhatu wants me alive.

126
00:14:08,377 --> 00:14:09,967
You just stay ready, Boran.

127
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:12,940
We will get rid of Böke at the first
opportunity.

128
00:14:12,940 --> 00:14:13,780
Then flee away.

129
00:14:14,151 --> 00:14:15,601
Understood, my Bey.

130
00:14:15,601 --> 00:14:16,411
Alişar Bey.

131
00:14:18,702 --> 00:14:20,552
Tell me...

132
00:14:20,552 --> 00:14:22,292
...what is happening, Alişar Bey?!

133
00:14:22,977 --> 00:14:25,327
You told me you would hand me Osman...

134
00:14:25,327 --> 00:14:27,717
...as well as you promised to avenge his
blood!

135
00:14:28,492 --> 00:14:29,642
Yes, I did.

136
00:14:31,070 --> 00:14:32,100
However...

137
00:14:33,670 --> 00:14:35,630
...Geyhatu is the one who wants
Osman.

138
00:14:37,739 --> 00:14:38,669
For what?

139
00:14:38,961 --> 00:14:42,961
Why can’t you still understand that Osman
is not alone, Dündar Bey?

140
00:14:44,554 --> 00:14:47,944
He wants to learn the one...

141
00:14:47,944 --> 00:14:49,864
...who is supporting him.

142
00:14:50,123 --> 00:14:53,253
Osman has been swimming in dirty waters
lately.

143
00:14:53,923 --> 00:14:55,973
I will personally take him to Konya.

144
00:14:57,282 --> 00:14:59,832
By the time Geyhatu is done with Osman…

145
00:14:59,832 --> 00:15:01,862
…you will stare him in the eyes.

146
00:15:04,316 --> 00:15:05,106
I promise.

147
00:15:06,124 --> 00:15:08,534
Two of us will go to Konya together.

148
00:15:10,927 --> 00:15:12,067
But...

149
00:15:12,590 --> 00:15:15,530
...first, we need to get done with our
business at the Tent.

150
00:15:16,265 --> 00:15:17,645
Do you understand?

151
00:15:17,862 --> 00:15:18,702
Uncle!

152
00:15:18,954 --> 00:15:22,124
I hope you don't bow your head and reach
that position...

153
00:15:22,124 --> 00:15:25,264
...where you disregard our ancestors by
trusting that Alişar dog.

154
00:15:25,264 --> 00:15:27,394
How can you still dare to talk?

155
00:15:28,716 --> 00:15:29,476
Huh?

156
00:15:30,128 --> 00:15:33,908
To take my revenge, I will find everyone
at the Tent who decided to join you...

157
00:15:33,908 --> 00:15:36,678
...thus got their hands dirty with my
son's blood.

158
00:15:37,784 --> 00:15:39,584
I will find and kill them all, Osman.

159
00:15:40,217 --> 00:15:41,137
Kill!

160
00:15:41,731 --> 00:15:42,701
All of them!

161
00:15:44,859 --> 00:15:45,909
Dündar Bey.

162
00:15:53,476 --> 00:15:55,026
Give me your soldiers.

163
00:15:55,333 --> 00:15:57,903
I will take Osman and his Alp to Konya.

164
00:15:58,093 --> 00:16:00,133
As you wish, Commander Böke.

165
00:16:22,135 --> 00:16:24,895
You can’t know how happy I am right now...

166
00:16:25,645 --> 00:16:28,595
...since you will not be attending our
wedding, Osman.

167
00:16:30,009 --> 00:16:31,329
Be careful, Alişar!

168
00:16:33,393 --> 00:16:36,543
You never know what's inside of a wedding
chest.

169
00:16:57,370 --> 00:16:59,580
The biggest danger there is...

170
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:00,900
...no longer exists.

171
00:17:03,630 --> 00:17:06,490
I’m leaving to get Zöhre Hatun.

172
00:17:06,855 --> 00:17:08,485
Wait for the news from me.

173
00:18:31,490 --> 00:18:33,890
My Bey, are we going to wait more to
take action?

174
00:18:33,890 --> 00:18:35,460
If needed, yes my brother.

175
00:18:37,068 --> 00:18:39,578
We will not compromise on our muslim
glory.

176
00:18:39,578 --> 00:18:42,408
We will never bow our heads for personal
benefits....

177
00:18:42,408 --> 00:18:43,838
...just like the letter 'Waw'.

178
00:18:45,669 --> 00:18:46,429
Enough!

179
00:18:47,596 --> 00:18:49,196
What are you keep talking about?

180
00:18:49,196 --> 00:18:51,446
You can not understand what
we speak of, Böke!

181
00:18:52,678 --> 00:18:55,988
We speak the language that turned
‘Kaysaria’ to 'Kayseri'.

182
00:18:55,988 --> 00:18:58,238
...and 'Ikoni' to Konya'.

183
00:19:00,205 --> 00:19:01,765
Stop mumbling, Osman.

184
00:19:02,921 --> 00:19:04,701
These are all fairy tales now.

185
00:19:06,352 --> 00:19:08,302
We will banish all of you like this.

186
00:19:10,617 --> 00:19:12,887
What you call fairy tales today...

187
00:19:12,887 --> 00:19:16,277
...are the very epics of tomorrows that
will haunt your people forever.

188
00:19:18,399 --> 00:19:21,159
Mongol storm have already started to
blow your fire out.

189
00:19:21,876 --> 00:19:24,956
We dominate every Turk there is
and continue our absolute reign.

190
00:19:27,755 --> 00:19:30,485
We are going to see if you will be
talkative like this...

191
00:19:30,485 --> 00:19:32,025
...once you meet mighty Geyhatu.

192
00:19:32,217 --> 00:19:34,107
You are in such a hurry, Böke.

193
00:19:35,206 --> 00:19:38,526
Every Turk tend to act like quenchless
sparkles of the hurricane.

194
00:19:40,388 --> 00:19:42,678
You may say we are less in numbers…

195
00:19:42,678 --> 00:19:44,538
…but even a single sparkling…

196
00:19:44,538 --> 00:19:47,068
…will be strong enough to burn down the
world.

197
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:52,582
Come on!

198
00:19:53,461 --> 00:19:55,501
No stopping till we get our horses!

199
00:20:15,299 --> 00:20:17,609
You all swim in deep waters, Kılıç Alp.

200
00:20:17,609 --> 00:20:19,879
You don’t care if you will drown or not.

201
00:20:19,879 --> 00:20:22,009
Don’t you worry about us, Zöhre Hatun.

202
00:20:22,789 --> 00:20:27,119
Osman Bey is tall enough and he can hold
his breath.

203
00:20:29,279 --> 00:20:30,789
What about his hands?

204
00:20:30,789 --> 00:20:32,809
Are they long enough to save you?

205
00:20:32,809 --> 00:20:33,559
My Bey!

206
00:20:35,412 --> 00:20:36,342
Dündar Bey.

207
00:20:39,342 --> 00:20:40,532
Yes, Dündar Bey!

208
00:20:41,707 --> 00:20:42,767
Dündar Bey...

209
00:20:42,767 --> 00:20:44,697
...whose privates you captured…

210
00:20:45,777 --> 00:20:49,397
...after you ambushed him while he was
carrying his daughter's wedding chest.

211
00:20:49,777 --> 00:20:50,557
Dündar Bey...

212
00:20:50,557 --> 00:20:52,047
...who you tortured.

213
00:20:52,478 --> 00:20:53,538
Bow your head!

214
00:21:08,071 --> 00:21:09,466
Just on time.

215
00:21:09,726 --> 00:21:10,726
Just on time...

216
00:21:10,766 --> 00:21:12,996
...you saved me from these
Shakirs, my Bey.

217
00:21:17,522 --> 00:21:20,192
May my life be sacrificed for your path.

218
00:21:24,126 --> 00:21:24,826
Osman?

219
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:27,183
Is he dead now?

220
00:21:27,183 --> 00:21:30,213
Instead of me, Geyhatu is going to kill
him.

221
00:21:31,939 --> 00:21:33,719
Don’t you worry about that.

222
00:21:34,818 --> 00:21:36,668
Our era has begun.

223
00:21:38,158 --> 00:21:39,418
Where is Bahadır?

224
00:21:39,717 --> 00:21:40,547
I just told you.

225
00:21:40,547 --> 00:21:42,487
Our era already has begun.

226
00:21:43,934 --> 00:21:45,924
Today is a blessed day.

227
00:21:46,784 --> 00:21:50,064
Bahadır is talking with Beys right now...

228
00:21:50,064 --> 00:21:52,074
...to lit the fire of rebellion..

229
00:21:53,274 --> 00:21:56,184
He will have everything ready.

230
00:21:57,921 --> 00:22:00,921
Today, for Gündüz and his followers...

231
00:22:00,921 --> 00:22:03,241
...the sun...

232
00:22:03,241 --> 00:22:04,831
...will set for the last time.

233
00:23:10,289 --> 00:23:14,532
Alişar Bey! Mother and father?
Please tell me they are alright.

234
00:23:15,230 --> 00:23:18,161
No one gets away with
something.

235
00:23:21,668 --> 00:23:23,786
Osman tired us with his madness...

236
00:23:24,331 --> 00:23:26,115
...his stupidness...

237
00:23:27,223 --> 00:23:28,963
...and his ambition.

238
00:23:30,304 --> 00:23:31,433
He wounded us.

239
00:23:33,921 --> 00:23:35,180
He killed us.

240
00:23:36,429 --> 00:23:38,387
Now he is marching to his
own end.

241
00:23:40,035 --> 00:23:43,211
And those who deserve to be
saved...

242
00:23:43,424 --> 00:23:44,575
...are saved.

243
00:23:46,585 --> 00:23:48,377
May your beautiful face smile.

244
00:23:49,264 --> 00:23:51,689
Your father went to take Zöhre Hatun.

245
00:23:52,832 --> 00:23:54,402
And Bahadır is on duty.

246
00:23:55,321 --> 00:23:56,824
They will be here soon.

247
00:23:58,797 --> 00:24:00,971
Thank Allah. Thank Allah.

248
00:24:02,805 --> 00:24:04,802
Thank you Alişar Bey, thank you.

249
00:24:06,638 --> 00:24:10,829
First, I shall reunite with my family.
Then, we'll take care of what is left.

250
00:24:12,183 --> 00:24:14,655
We'll take revenge for my brother.

251
00:24:17,430 --> 00:24:21,284
I don't know what could we do
without you, Alişar Bey.

252
00:24:24,918 --> 00:24:26,852
May Allah Bless you.

253
00:24:27,092 --> 00:24:29,066
My beautiful Aygül Hatun.

254
00:24:29,358 --> 00:24:32,327
Now that you are here...

255
00:24:35,013 --> 00:24:37,003
...my mansion is finally home.

256
00:24:45,239 --> 00:24:48,569
I know many days that I returned to
this mansion with distress.

257
00:24:49,724 --> 00:24:55,151
But never did the sun shined that
bright when I stepped inside.

258
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:00,370
Thank Allah.

259
00:25:02,777 --> 00:25:04,528
Not at all.

260
00:25:06,292 --> 00:25:07,637
If you'll allow me...

261
00:25:08,248 --> 00:25:09,881
I have some matters to attend to.

262
00:25:10,137 --> 00:25:11,972
Then we can sit and talk.

263
00:25:13,061 --> 00:25:14,563
Alişar Bey.

264
00:25:17,330 --> 00:25:19,472
Where is Osman Bey?

265
00:25:21,571 --> 00:25:23,528
Is he still alive?

266
00:25:25,756 --> 00:25:27,784
Osman is on his way to Konya.

267
00:25:29,051 --> 00:25:31,358
He'll be interrogated by Geyhatu.

268
00:25:33,722 --> 00:25:34,522
But...

269
00:25:36,012 --> 00:25:37,941
...if a man gets interrogated...

270
00:25:38,196 --> 00:25:40,994
...personally by Geyhatu...

271
00:25:42,387 --> 00:25:44,592
...there won't be much left of him after.

272
00:26:10,867 --> 00:26:13,225
Where is Osman Bey?

273
00:26:13,802 --> 00:26:15,004
Speak!

274
00:26:17,060 --> 00:26:19,640
If you speak, I'll make it quick.
Without pain.

275
00:26:20,856 --> 00:26:22,572
Where is Osman Bey?

276
00:26:33,399 --> 00:26:36,078
I saved your life again, Kongar!

277
00:26:46,358 --> 00:26:49,170
Why haven't you kill this one?

278
00:26:53,627 --> 00:26:56,617
He knows where Osman is but
doesn't speak.

279
00:26:58,863 --> 00:27:03,854
Where is Osman? If you don't speak now,
I'll skin you alive!

280
00:27:04,396 --> 00:27:08,652
Böke took him. They are going to Konya.

281
00:27:09,167 --> 00:27:11,984
They are taking him to Geyhatu.

282
00:27:33,897 --> 00:27:35,292
Let's move fast.

283
00:27:37,102 --> 00:27:38,877
Balgay awaits.

284
00:28:17,412 --> 00:28:21,190
How did you learn about the Monks of
Margareth?

285
00:28:23,900 --> 00:28:29,130
Your uncle, Sungurtekin, was it him who
informed you?

286
00:28:41,165 --> 00:28:43,191
Speak, Osman.

287
00:28:44,153 --> 00:28:46,723
Or I'll make this trip way harder for you.

288
00:28:52,425 --> 00:28:54,999
Where is Princess Adelfa?

289
00:29:06,250 --> 00:29:09,431
Nobody gave you as much as trouble...

290
00:29:09,698 --> 00:29:11,720
...as the children of Süleyman Ghazi...

291
00:29:11,981 --> 00:29:13,871
...my grandfather.

292
00:29:16,781 --> 00:29:18,661
This is just a beginning.

293
00:29:19,995 --> 00:29:22,330
I won't tell you what I know.

294
00:29:23,131 --> 00:29:25,659
You should think about yourself.

295
00:29:26,979 --> 00:29:29,471
Speak, Osman. Speak!

296
00:29:38,432 --> 00:29:41,375
Geyhatu would never let someone as
incapable as you, alive.

297
00:29:43,296 --> 00:29:46,810
When we reach Konya, you'll be first
to be beheaded.

298
00:30:41,590 --> 00:30:43,183
Enough!

299
00:30:46,477 --> 00:30:48,137
You'll kill him.

300
00:30:59,711 --> 00:31:02,143
I'll see you dead, Osman.

301
00:31:10,452 --> 00:31:12,568
Take him.

302
00:31:45,963 --> 00:31:55,361
May dark shamans mount wind horses
and come.

303
00:31:56,673 --> 00:32:03,104
Today is for revenge.

304
00:32:05,536 --> 00:32:14,563
Today is for bringing dark curses
to blue skies.

305
00:33:56,871 --> 00:34:00,068
My valiant warrior, Kongar!

306
00:34:02,498 --> 00:34:04,833
What happened in my absence?

307
00:34:06,139 --> 00:34:09,295
What news have you brought me
about Osman?

308
00:34:10,146 --> 00:34:14,260
Böke and Alişar captured Osman.

309
00:34:15,573 --> 00:34:17,837
And now they are moving to Konya.

310
00:34:20,817 --> 00:34:22,993
He is taking Osman to Geyhatu.

311
00:34:34,129 --> 00:34:35,789
Geyhatu...

312
00:34:36,725 --> 00:34:41,625
...who sold his soul to Budha in
Buddhist temples can't have Osman.

313
00:34:43,241 --> 00:34:48,048
That ignoble who lost his dignity...

314
00:34:49,331 --> 00:34:53,132
...that dog who tried to go over the
might of Tengri...

315
00:34:54,030 --> 00:35:01,160
...can't take possession of Genghis' Laws.
He can't! He can't!

316
00:35:12,878 --> 00:35:14,371
What happened in Konya?

317
00:35:16,800 --> 00:35:19,177
Osman deceived Balgay.

318
00:35:21,431 --> 00:35:23,259
Documents weren't real.

319
00:35:26,009 --> 00:35:28,329
To make a feint, he must know
of the real one.

320
00:35:29,369 --> 00:35:32,507
Otherwise, he wouldn't be able
to make a faint and deceive me.

321
00:35:34,337 --> 00:35:37,924
I'll take Genghis Khan's Laws from
Osman's hands.

322
00:35:39,534 --> 00:35:43,227
He'll pay for the disgrace he gave me.

323
00:35:46,953 --> 00:35:50,411
What did Geyhatu do when he found
out that the documents were fake?

324
00:35:50,878 --> 00:35:52,738
He decided on execution.

325
00:35:53,544 --> 00:35:54,784
For all of us.

326
00:35:57,052 --> 00:35:59,788
If we want to survive, only thing
we need to do is...

327
00:36:00,947 --> 00:36:03,200
...taking the documents back from Osman.

328
00:36:04,348 --> 00:36:07,383
Or Geyhatu will finish us off, sooner
or later.

329
00:36:16,564 --> 00:36:19,252
We'll get Osman from Böke's hands.

330
00:36:20,108 --> 00:36:22,149
We should go to Konya road fastly.

331
00:36:22,618 --> 00:36:24,219
Don't underestimate Böke.

332
00:36:25,441 --> 00:36:28,852
He is smart enough...

333
00:36:29,759 --> 00:36:31,280
...not go on the main road.

334
00:36:33,278 --> 00:36:36,302
The path our spies use,
he'll use that one.

335
00:36:37,040 --> 00:36:38,278
Exactly.

336
00:36:40,001 --> 00:36:41,651
They'll go that way.

337
00:36:42,541 --> 00:36:43,837
We are leaving.

338
00:36:45,036 --> 00:36:47,264
We'll get Osman before Geyhatu does.

339
00:37:19,474 --> 00:37:21,069
Elders of Kayı...

340
00:37:21,253 --> 00:37:23,255
...future of the Tent...

341
00:37:23,949 --> 00:37:25,830
...my father sent his regards.

342
00:37:28,228 --> 00:37:29,977
Thank Allah.

343
00:37:30,787 --> 00:37:32,253
Is he healthy?

344
00:37:32,482 --> 00:37:33,694
Yes, thank Allah.

345
00:37:33,963 --> 00:37:36,726
But Osman tried to kill him, again.

346
00:37:38,130 --> 00:37:40,219
But this time, we broke all
his plans.

347
00:37:40,963 --> 00:37:43,724
We captured him and...

348
00:37:43,828 --> 00:37:46,122
...sent him with Böke to Geyhatu
for execution.

349
00:37:46,253 --> 00:37:48,345
Time for rebellion has come, then.

350
00:37:48,619 --> 00:37:49,622
It has.

351
00:37:50,710 --> 00:37:51,998
And it's now.

352
00:37:52,158 --> 00:37:55,160
Wouldn't a night attack be wiser?

353
00:37:55,370 --> 00:37:57,289
You take the lead if you desire.

354
00:37:58,070 --> 00:37:59,823
And we'll follow you. Demirci Bey.

355
00:38:00,384 --> 00:38:03,382
Not at all, my Bey. Whatever Dündar Bey
says is okay.

356
00:38:05,132 --> 00:38:07,517
The alps following you, are they in the
forest?

357
00:38:08,140 --> 00:38:10,923
Bamsı Bey doesn't let anyone move
in the Tents.

358
00:38:11,922 --> 00:38:15,133
So, they have been waiting for our
word for a while.

359
00:38:16,559 --> 00:38:18,003
Good.

360
00:38:18,862 --> 00:38:20,657
Ready the horses.

361
00:38:21,737 --> 00:38:24,071
We'll poke Bamsı Bey's eyes.

362
00:38:25,539 --> 00:38:28,575
And we'll have Gündüz's head on a spike!

363
00:38:29,686 --> 00:38:32,513
We have been dreaming of that day for
a while.

364
00:38:33,351 --> 00:38:36,542
May Allah protect our Dündar Bey.

365
00:38:36,964 --> 00:38:38,053
Amin.

366
00:38:39,856 --> 00:38:44,125
His brother will leave the tents after
realizing the absence of Osman.

367
00:38:45,693 --> 00:38:48,325
After all, a hunter is a prey...

368
00:38:49,031 --> 00:38:50,823
...as much as he is a hunter.

369
00:39:13,256 --> 00:39:16,039
What's wrong, Konur?
What's this hurry?

370
00:39:16,216 --> 00:39:18,694
My Bey, we went to Osman Bey's place.

371
00:39:18,792 --> 00:39:20,392
Kılıç Alp was dead.

372
00:39:23,871 --> 00:39:25,622
-Kılıç.
-Kılıç.

373
00:39:27,075 --> 00:39:29,203
What are you saying, son?

374
00:39:30,037 --> 00:39:32,870
Gündüz, Gündüz...
It doesn't look good at all.

375
00:39:33,455 --> 00:39:36,742
Snakes are on charge!

376
00:39:37,309 --> 00:39:39,350
We shouldn't just stand.

377
00:39:39,984 --> 00:39:42,658
Abdurrahman Ghazi, the Tent is
under your protection.

378
00:39:42,750 --> 00:39:44,589
Don't worry, Gündüz.

379
00:39:44,662 --> 00:39:47,040
As long as you are here, I don't.

380
00:39:47,110 --> 00:39:49,170
Tell the soldiers to take battle position.

381
00:39:49,191 --> 00:39:51,941
Tell women to get ready.

382
00:39:54,428 --> 00:39:55,929
C'mon, c'mon.

383
00:40:07,094 --> 00:40:08,132
Come on.

384
00:40:23,533 --> 00:40:24,989
Don't be sad.

385
00:40:26,126 --> 00:40:28,843
All these hustles is for you...

386
00:40:33,961 --> 00:40:36,078
All the grief is behind us.

387
00:40:37,253 --> 00:40:39,936
And until they speak--

388
00:40:41,136 --> 00:40:44,400
From now, I won't let anything
upset you.

389
00:40:45,410 --> 00:40:46,656
You should know.

390
00:40:47,116 --> 00:40:51,102
I can't help it, Alişar Bey.
I can't feel good before seeing them.

391
00:40:51,276 --> 00:40:52,905
Forgive me.

392
00:41:00,117 --> 00:41:01,148
Mother!

393
00:41:03,025 --> 00:41:04,036
Father!

394
00:41:05,836 --> 00:41:07,705
Thank Allah, you are okay.

395
00:41:08,245 --> 00:41:11,975
Thank Allah, that he didn't leave
us alone on this holy day.

396
00:41:13,464 --> 00:41:16,919
We are fine, daughter. Osman
had fallen to his own trap.

397
00:41:18,071 --> 00:41:20,520
As you see, we are here,
safe and sound.

398
00:41:21,095 --> 00:41:23,608
-Don't worry.
-He hoped for my help.

399
00:41:23,768 --> 00:41:25,708
But I didn't believe his fancy words.

400
00:41:26,824 --> 00:41:28,812
He said that we are the same blood...

401
00:41:29,528 --> 00:41:31,592
He tries to blind our eyes
with lies.

402
00:41:31,921 --> 00:41:34,281
Just a little longer, daughter...

403
00:41:34,521 --> 00:41:36,841
...every single one of them...

404
00:41:38,321 --> 00:41:40,261
...will pay for what they have done.

405
00:41:42,921 --> 00:41:46,295
-Any news from Bahadır?
-He is on duty.

406
00:41:47,593 --> 00:41:52,536
All the preparations are done.
And now you are here, too.

407
00:41:53,957 --> 00:41:55,999
Order will come to the Tent...

408
00:41:56,568 --> 00:41:59,208
...and happiness will come to my mansion.

409
00:42:39,005 --> 00:42:41,008
Tie them to a tree.

410
00:42:41,248 --> 00:42:42,618
And whip them until--

411
00:43:18,932 --> 00:43:21,289
Balgay...

412
00:43:32,007 --> 00:43:33,429
Balgay!

413
00:45:09,396 --> 00:45:10,776
Thank Allah.

414
00:45:10,815 --> 00:45:15,885
Gündüz and Bamsı left. We know
who'll stick our from the people as well.

415
00:45:16,106 --> 00:45:20,936
Everything will be easier
than we think, Demirci Bey.

416
00:45:22,299 --> 00:45:26,299
Only Abdurrahman Gazi is left.

417
00:45:26,925 --> 00:45:30,645
It's over once we deal with him.

418
00:45:36,961 --> 00:45:38,301
Bismillah.

419
00:45:56,480 --> 00:45:59,140
You're a lucky guy, Abdurrahman Gazi.

420
00:46:05,606 --> 00:46:09,066
You won't be passing to the other side
without ablutions.

421
00:46:09,741 --> 00:46:13,881
- Not so easy.
- Let's see.

422
00:46:17,081 --> 00:46:18,931
Coem to your death!

423
00:46:20,449 --> 00:46:22,519
Bring it on, Şahin Bey!

424
00:46:28,865 --> 00:46:30,005
Allah!

425
00:46:43,885 --> 00:46:47,405
I spent my life cutting traitors like you!

426
00:46:49,443 --> 00:46:50,603
Come on!

427
00:46:51,856 --> 00:46:52,926
Come on!

428
00:47:12,143 --> 00:47:13,113
Stop!

429
00:47:22,973 --> 00:47:27,653
Stop, Abdurrahman Gazi.
Don't do the same mistake we did.

430
00:47:32,383 --> 00:47:33,383
Get up!

431
00:47:41,564 --> 00:47:44,654
Take them! Put them in the caged tent!

432
00:47:45,382 --> 00:47:48,762
Gündüz Bey will judge them.

433
00:48:09,651 --> 00:48:12,351
You promised to stay loyal to me and...

434
00:48:12,351 --> 00:48:15,491
... you've destroyed your
promise twice, Osman.

435
00:48:17,033 --> 00:48:19,773
Genghis Khan's laws were fake.

436
00:48:20,355 --> 00:48:28,135
You humiliated me to Geyhatu
in front of all his soldiers in Konya!

437
00:48:30,430 --> 00:48:37,740
That's better. You saw that
we're loyal to no one but Allah.

438
00:48:49,216 --> 00:48:52,516
We'll stay here until...

439
00:48:52,516 --> 00:48:59,976
... what you know comes out of your
mouth, and your spirit leaves your flesh.

440
00:49:04,510 --> 00:49:09,740
I can't see how strong you are
while my hands are tied, Balgay.

441
00:49:10,751 --> 00:49:14,751
Untie me so I can cool your
anger down in your blood!

442
00:49:16,730 --> 00:49:20,260
You're a corpse for me now.

443
00:49:21,243 --> 00:49:25,613
A corpse that lives until
I get the words from it's mouth!

444
00:49:29,950 --> 00:49:32,150
My Bey! My Bey!

445
00:50:10,706 --> 00:50:17,216
Because of your incompetence,
Geyhatu decided to execute you.

446
00:50:23,416 --> 00:50:25,746
I'll kill you before him!

447
00:50:25,746 --> 00:50:29,156
Forgive me! Almighty Balgay.

448
00:50:30,185 --> 00:50:31,635
Forgive me...

449
00:50:34,447 --> 00:50:36,437
... so I can serve you.

450
00:50:41,771 --> 00:50:45,771
My Bey! What are we going to do?

451
00:50:53,651 --> 00:50:55,821
Take Boran out of here.

452
00:50:58,795 --> 00:51:01,715
Boran? How?

453
00:51:02,283 --> 00:51:03,873
Listen to me, brother.

454
00:51:06,708 --> 00:51:11,188
Do you agree to be my slave,
in exchange for your life?

455
00:51:11,213 --> 00:51:15,213
I agree. I agree, Almighty Balgay.

456
00:51:22,218 --> 00:51:23,398
I agree.

457
00:51:35,219 --> 00:51:41,749
Then, you'll be on my side
with Nökers against Geyhatu.

458
00:51:45,467 --> 00:51:51,407
Sharp teeth of a dog like you
mean the world to me.

459
00:51:53,079 --> 00:51:56,779
It's my victory against Geyhatu.

460
00:52:06,266 --> 00:52:12,996
Give Böke his weapons.
And hang Osman to that tree.

461
00:52:15,742 --> 00:52:16,982
My Bey!

462
00:53:13,210 --> 00:53:14,790
- Son!
- Yes, my Bey?

463
00:53:16,831 --> 00:53:20,831
Check the Tent's entrance trenches.
We must not lack anything.

464
00:53:21,099 --> 00:53:24,789
Fill the quivers.
We need those arrows ready.

465
00:53:24,789 --> 00:53:26,929
- Right away, my Bey.
- Go!

466
00:53:46,489 --> 00:53:49,209
What is it, Selcan Hatun?
Where are you going?

467
00:53:49,209 --> 00:53:52,119
I'll visit our Sheikh, Abdurrahman Gazi.

468
00:53:52,485 --> 00:53:55,475
I'd like to inform him of our situation
and get his blessings.

469
00:53:55,995 --> 00:53:59,995
I'll send an Alp with you,
don't go out there all alone.

470
00:54:00,111 --> 00:54:02,561
We're dependent on Allah...

471
00:54:02,561 --> 00:54:05,591
... whether if we have an Alp with
us or not, Abdurrahman Gazi.

472
00:54:08,184 --> 00:54:12,184
Thank you. You need those valiants.
Don't worry about me.

473
00:54:12,317 --> 00:54:18,187
Thank you.
Send our best regards to our Sheikh.

474
00:54:19,822 --> 00:54:21,712
He shall pray for us.

475
00:54:57,315 --> 00:55:01,315
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim
(in the name of God, the merciful and compassionate.)

476
00:55:33,161 --> 00:55:36,981
May Allah allow us to complete
every duty with faith...

477
00:55:37,894 --> 00:55:41,894
... to tame our desires...

478
00:55:43,038 --> 00:55:49,498
... to see the days this lodge
will be enlightened by the light of Islam.

479
00:55:50,803 --> 00:55:52,443
Amen, my Sheikh.

480
00:56:06,005 --> 00:56:12,745
Now you tell me. You left
the Tent with the duty we gave you.

481
00:56:13,429 --> 00:56:16,659
You were going to be our eyes
and ears there.

482
00:56:17,178 --> 00:56:20,808
You were going to bring us the news
if something happened.

483
00:56:22,874 --> 00:56:27,674
Why did you run out of patience
so you've returned, Bala?

484
00:56:29,308 --> 00:56:31,288
My Sheikh, I thought...

485
00:56:34,246 --> 00:56:38,376
... I will be more useful to you if
I stay by your side.

486
00:56:39,216 --> 00:56:42,736
I'll have done something
better for myself.

487
00:56:46,446 --> 00:56:50,616
You came here looking for
something better for yourself.

488
00:56:52,562 --> 00:56:55,342
Why couldn't you find
such a thing in the Tent?

489
00:56:55,484 --> 00:56:59,484
No, everyone in the Tent is alright.

490
00:57:00,321 --> 00:57:02,781
I didn't hear a single bad
word from anyone.

491
00:57:03,142 --> 00:57:08,152
Selcan mother, Gündüz Bey, and Bamsı
Bey all protect me, bless them.

492
00:57:11,397 --> 00:57:13,387
What about Osman Bey?

493
00:57:13,387 --> 00:57:15,567
What is he doing?

494
00:57:21,965 --> 00:57:24,285
I don't know what Osman Bey
is doing, my Sheikh.

495
00:57:25,779 --> 00:57:28,859
Only those who hear from him
know what he's doing.

496
00:57:29,463 --> 00:57:31,953
But he is bad with his uncle.

497
00:57:34,225 --> 00:57:36,955
Dündar Bey espoused his daughter
with Alişar Bey.

498
00:57:37,919 --> 00:57:40,389
Their last argument was because of this.

499
00:57:42,899 --> 00:57:44,279
Osman Bey...

500
00:57:46,001 --> 00:57:49,041
... doesn't want Aygül to marry Alişar.

501
00:57:51,450 --> 00:57:53,400
I don't know the rest.

502
00:58:02,424 --> 00:58:09,734
Forgive me. I couldn't stay there.
I couldn't be away from you, father.

503
00:58:14,446 --> 00:58:19,126
Okay then.
Let's say the child missed her father.

504
00:58:20,703 --> 00:58:26,283
I personally never heard that
you left a duty incomplete...

505
00:58:27,063 --> 00:58:31,187
... cried out when you
ran out of patience...

506
00:58:31,383 --> 00:58:34,803
... or act impulsively.

507
00:58:54,381 --> 00:58:56,041
Keep going.

508
00:59:20,782 --> 00:59:23,142
Ambush! Its an ambush!

509
00:59:29,444 --> 00:59:31,104
Come on!

510
00:59:55,220 --> 00:59:59,220
Alps! What are you doing?

511
01:00:00,746 --> 01:00:02,976
End of the road, Gündüz!

512
01:00:10,444 --> 01:00:15,624
Dündar left the tent.
But his ears are still here.

513
01:00:16,285 --> 01:00:22,355
What I'm trying to say is that
we need to watch our words near Bahadır

514
01:00:27,287 --> 01:00:29,617
The bird of death landed on you.

515
01:00:29,617 --> 01:00:34,357
While Osman is dying in Konya,
you'll die in my hands!

516
01:00:34,995 --> 01:00:41,565
Gündüz! Leave Bahadır to me!
Leave Bahadır to me.

517
01:00:44,032 --> 01:00:46,302
So, was everything a game, Bahadır?

518
01:00:46,302 --> 01:00:51,702
Yes. But the games are over.
Attack!

519
01:00:55,288 --> 01:00:57,468
We're here, Gündüz Bey!

520
01:01:09,802 --> 01:01:11,842
What are you waiting for? Attack!

521
01:02:20,988 --> 01:02:23,438
Bahadır! Bahadır!

522
01:02:27,047 --> 01:02:28,227
Stop!

523
01:02:32,310 --> 01:02:34,160
Stop, Bahadır!

524
01:02:36,202 --> 01:02:40,202
Bamsı Bey! Your age is over!

525
01:02:41,080 --> 01:02:43,980
Give up! Let's solve
this without spilling any blood.

526
01:02:44,179 --> 01:02:52,779
Look, son. You're the grandson
of the great Süleyman Şah.

527
01:02:59,745 --> 01:03:03,855
Don't make me take your life.

528
01:03:05,055 --> 01:03:08,165
Get out of this pit that you're in!
Open your eyes!

529
01:03:08,165 --> 01:03:11,405
Stop following your father!
Right, son?

530
01:03:36,846 --> 01:03:38,646
You asked for it, Bamsı Bey!

531
01:03:49,984 --> 01:03:51,454
Bahadır!

532
01:03:52,844 --> 01:03:56,844
I'll tell you one last time.
Apologise, Bahadır!

533
01:03:57,523 --> 01:04:03,933
Apologise! Stop this infidelity.
So that I don't kill you.

534
01:04:04,269 --> 01:04:06,329
So I don't kill you.

535
01:04:07,506 --> 01:04:13,906
Bamsı Bey! Don't you see?
Your age is over!

536
01:04:14,400 --> 01:04:20,820
It's over! The Alps you've trusted are
fighting against you today, Bamsı Bey!

537
01:04:30,473 --> 01:04:34,473
You don't understand!
You don't!

538
01:04:36,318 --> 01:04:40,318
The age of those who tell the truth
never ends!

539
01:04:42,356 --> 01:04:45,396
We'll always be alive!

540
01:04:46,815 --> 01:04:52,365
Your weapons can't penetrate
our armour, you fool!

541
01:04:52,635 --> 01:04:57,715
It can't! You'll drown in that
well of betrayal.

542
01:04:58,153 --> 01:05:05,943
Every night, you'll wait for someone in
your own Tent to kill you, Bamsı Bey.

543
01:05:06,382 --> 01:05:12,362
I pity you, Bamsı Bey. Surrender.
Switch to our side.

544
01:05:12,839 --> 01:05:15,949
So that you can live the rest of
your days in comfort, Bamsı Bey.

545
01:05:17,058 --> 01:05:21,058
Do you think we're after comfort,
you fool?

546
01:05:23,699 --> 01:05:27,119
We're not afraid of death, thank Allah!

547
01:05:27,441 --> 01:05:32,761
But your kind will live their lives
running away like dogs!

548
01:05:32,886 --> 01:05:36,616
Your corpses will be buried in
the graveyard of traitors!

549
01:06:18,608 --> 01:06:21,578
Geyhatu beat you up well.

550
01:06:23,419 --> 01:06:25,869
Apparent from your anger.

551
01:06:33,336 --> 01:06:39,366
Did those spirits and the bugs
you worship turn their backs to you?

552
01:06:42,517 --> 01:06:49,957
I'm not in a hurry.
You'll eventually talk.

553
01:08:16,211 --> 01:08:19,141
My Bey!

554
01:08:32,458 --> 01:08:36,778
Those will stay on around
your neck until you talk!

555
01:08:47,498 --> 01:08:51,128
My Bey! Hang on, my Bey!
Hang on!

556
01:09:12,134 --> 01:09:13,364
Let him go!

557
01:09:17,946 --> 01:09:22,646
I'm here, my Bey!
Hang on, my Bey!

558
01:09:27,206 --> 01:09:28,466
Hang on!

559
01:09:36,602 --> 01:09:38,142
Hang on, my Bey!

560
01:10:04,054 --> 01:10:05,134
Talk!

561
01:10:21,832 --> 01:10:22,822
My Bey!

562
01:11:09,482 --> 01:11:10,602
Let him go.

563
01:11:31,609 --> 01:11:32,769
Talk.

564
01:12:02,193 --> 01:12:07,553
You will tell me where
Genghis Khan's laws are!

565
01:12:08,625 --> 01:12:12,005
You will tell me who
you got the laws from!

566
01:12:12,715 --> 01:12:18,545
You will tell me who
the secret power behind you is!

567
01:12:19,545 --> 01:12:22,605
Now or never!

568
01:12:30,889 --> 01:12:35,089
My Bey!
Let me go!

569
01:12:47,668 --> 01:12:53,148
I wi-- I w--
I will talk...

570
01:13:05,984 --> 01:13:07,024
My Bey!

571
01:13:09,959 --> 01:13:13,149
I'll talk...
I will talk...

572
01:13:13,569 --> 01:13:18,999
No negotiating, no trust.
You'll tell me everything you know.

573
01:13:19,888 --> 01:13:28,008
That rope will stay on your neck
until I get Genghis Khan's laws!

574
01:13:30,344 --> 01:13:35,454
If your Alp runs out of strength, you
won't have anywhere to step on.

575
01:13:36,468 --> 01:13:38,738
I won't save you, know that.

576
01:13:39,076 --> 01:13:41,046
Allahu Akbar! ( Allah is the greatest!)

577
01:13:42,993 --> 01:13:47,293
Not only Genghis Khan's laws...

578
01:13:48,803 --> 01:13:53,793
... I know everything about you
and your dogs.

579
01:13:56,477 --> 01:14:00,737
You're trying to deceive me again, Osman.

580
01:14:02,025 --> 01:14:06,375
But this time, I won't trust you.

581
01:14:07,269 --> 01:14:13,359
You'll bring me the laws
I want to me, now!

582
01:14:14,186 --> 01:14:18,766
Since you don't believe me,
let me convince you.

583
01:14:21,121 --> 01:14:22,931
For example...

584
01:14:28,552 --> 01:14:30,452
Kongar...

585
01:14:39,361 --> 01:14:41,391
What about Kongar?

586
01:14:43,347 --> 01:14:50,167
How you bought him from a slave market...
How you made him your slave...

587
01:14:52,057 --> 01:14:53,777
For example...

588
01:14:53,864 --> 01:14:55,804
... we can start from here.

589
01:15:08,599 --> 01:15:09,919
Kongar!

590
01:15:25,181 --> 01:15:30,111
How do you know this?
Who told you this?

591
01:15:32,081 --> 01:15:37,941
If I'm lying,
why are you afraid that Kongar will hear?

592
01:15:38,634 --> 01:15:40,904
How do you know this?

593
01:15:45,476 --> 01:15:47,666
Emperor of Byzantium.

594
01:15:55,685 --> 01:15:59,685
My only alliance is with him.

595
01:16:16,591 --> 01:16:23,051
Come on! Come here.
Come on.

596
01:17:12,752 --> 01:17:14,342
Burçin Hatun?

597
01:17:16,885 --> 01:17:18,345
My daughter?

598
01:17:56,543 --> 01:17:58,623
Aybars!

599
01:18:04,120 --> 01:18:07,300
Burçin! My daughter!

600
01:18:09,421 --> 01:18:17,371
Your fiance Aybars couldn't meet his
love in this world, but...

601
01:18:19,866 --> 01:18:25,136
... he met his eternal love.

602
01:18:26,168 --> 01:18:30,168
My daughter... Burçin...

603
01:18:31,877 --> 01:18:34,927
Your meeting...

604
01:18:37,359 --> 01:18:39,669
... will be on the doomsday.

605
01:18:45,953 --> 01:18:47,173
Burçin...

606
01:18:52,670 --> 01:18:54,040
My daughter...

607
01:18:56,773 --> 01:18:58,083
Why?

608
01:19:04,666 --> 01:19:05,586
Why?

609
01:19:14,335 --> 01:19:15,515
At last.

610
01:19:24,797 --> 01:19:27,487
You'll get what you deserve, Bamsı Bey!

611
01:19:39,087 --> 01:19:41,187
We're here, Bamsı Bey!

612
01:20:00,120 --> 01:20:01,870
Bamsı Bey!

613
01:20:05,830 --> 01:20:10,440
Bamsı Bey! Are you okay?
- Are you okay?

614
01:20:13,376 --> 01:20:17,266
Bamsı Bey! Who did this to you?

615
01:20:17,266 --> 01:20:22,196
Was it Bahadır?
I'll strangle him myself!

616
01:20:24,143 --> 01:20:27,653
Dümrul! Aras! What are you waiting for?
Go start a fire!

617
01:20:27,653 --> 01:20:29,733
- We need to take these arrows out.
- No!

618
01:20:29,733 --> 01:20:33,663
We can't do that now!
We'll take him to the Tent.

619
01:20:33,985 --> 01:20:37,475
Konur! Go chase that traitor!

620
01:20:37,794 --> 01:20:42,264
If you return without killing him, I will
kill you, know that! Go!

621
01:20:42,264 --> 01:20:43,254
Konur!

622
01:20:45,439 --> 01:20:47,009
My Bey?

623
01:20:50,709 --> 01:20:51,759
My Bey.

624
01:20:56,798 --> 01:20:57,798
Burçin...

625
01:20:58,715 --> 01:20:59,945
My daughter...

626
01:21:20,253 --> 01:21:23,773
My Aybars' fiance...

627
01:21:26,784 --> 01:21:28,914
... did this to me, Konur.

628
01:21:40,127 --> 01:21:44,127
- Gündüz...
- Bamsı Bey...

629
01:21:45,565 --> 01:21:48,985
Burçin shot me...
Burçin...

630
01:21:50,496 --> 01:21:52,226
My daughter shot me.

631
01:22:03,809 --> 01:22:07,809
But! But...

632
01:22:16,385 --> 01:22:17,505
Now...

633
01:22:20,057 --> 01:22:22,067
If my Aybars...

634
01:22:23,582 --> 01:22:28,242
... comes out of his grave...

635
01:22:28,242 --> 01:22:30,267
Don't, Bamsı Bey.

636
01:22:37,284 --> 01:22:39,424
I've made the judgement.

637
01:22:40,596 --> 01:22:42,326
I've made the judgement.

638
01:22:43,526 --> 01:22:45,646
- Don't, Bamsı Bey.
- Gündüz...

639
01:22:46,339 --> 01:22:48,359
I've made the judgement.

640
01:22:49,084 --> 01:22:52,014
- Let's chase them!
- Don't, Bamsı Bey!

641
01:22:52,531 --> 01:22:55,631
- Lets chase--
- Bamsı Bey, stop!

642
01:23:33,629 --> 01:23:35,539
My daughter shot me.

643
01:23:36,879 --> 01:23:38,679
Burçin shot me.

644
01:23:45,697 --> 01:23:47,097
Burçin shot me.

645
01:23:49,428 --> 01:23:51,048
My daughter did.

646
01:23:59,033 --> 01:24:00,743
My daughter shot me.

647
01:24:04,143 --> 01:24:06,183
My daughter shot me.

648
01:24:09,002 --> 01:24:10,972
My daughter shot me.

649
01:24:30,267 --> 01:24:35,017
- Burçin Hatun! I owe you my life!
- Hurry up, Bahadır Bey!

650
01:24:35,017 --> 01:24:38,972
- They'll catch up to us.
- Come with me. Don't go to the Tent.

651
01:24:38,972 --> 01:24:40,872
They'll torture you there.

652
01:24:42,217 --> 01:24:44,617
My home is where you are.

653
01:24:54,423 --> 01:24:55,733
Let's go.

654
01:25:00,555 --> 01:25:05,795
You made an agreement with
the Emperor to stop...

655
01:25:06,925 --> 01:25:10,425
... the Monks of Margaret from
taking over the palace.

656
01:25:11,772 --> 01:25:15,772
I was protecting my Tent.
And he was protecting his throne.

657
01:25:22,606 --> 01:25:27,456
The secret powers behind me
were his spies.

658
01:25:28,344 --> 01:25:33,384
They told me everything about you
and your dogs.

659
01:25:41,719 --> 01:25:43,239
Prove it.

660
01:25:46,939 --> 01:25:47,989
Then...

661
01:25:49,569 --> 01:25:51,319
... bring me down.

662
01:25:53,745 --> 01:25:55,205
Bring him down slowly.

663
01:26:01,707 --> 01:26:03,087
My Bey!

664
01:27:18,506 --> 01:27:24,126
What is an agreement I've made
with a slave trader years ago...

665
01:27:24,792 --> 01:27:27,372
... doing in your hands?

666
01:27:30,485 --> 01:27:32,815
What kind of capability is this?

667
01:27:33,375 --> 01:27:34,785
I told you.

668
01:27:39,185 --> 01:27:43,545
Both the Emperor and
his spies are with me.

669
01:27:44,403 --> 01:27:45,843
I'm not alone.

670
01:27:47,464 --> 01:27:52,624
Then tell me where
the Genghis' Laws that you're hiding are.

671
01:27:54,755 --> 01:27:57,035
Geyhatu will come here.

672
01:27:58,083 --> 01:28:01,703
To protect my Tent from his wrath...

673
01:28:03,723 --> 01:28:06,223
... you will let me live.

674
01:28:07,068 --> 01:28:10,248
I said no agreements! No, no, no!

675
01:28:11,141 --> 01:28:17,241
If you don't kill me, I will give you
such an information about Geyhatu...

676
01:28:18,530 --> 01:28:22,530
... that you'll take him down from
his throne and take his place.

677
01:28:25,244 --> 01:28:29,374
That rope will stay on your neck...

678
01:28:29,951 --> 01:28:33,951
... until I get the laws I want!

679
01:28:36,317 --> 01:28:37,547
Agreed.

680
01:28:40,990 --> 01:28:47,230
If I'm telling the truth, we'll both win.

681
01:28:53,219 --> 01:28:54,499
Boran...

682
01:29:00,579 --> 01:29:03,379
Bring the laws.

683
01:29:06,016 --> 01:29:11,760
Cerkutay! Take the soldiers and
bring the laws to me.

684
01:29:11,760 --> 01:29:16,708
Commander Balgay, if you allow me,
I want to take this dog.

685
01:29:16,708 --> 01:29:21,828
If they try to trick us again,
I want to punish them.

686
01:29:31,535 --> 01:29:33,465
Go.

687
01:29:35,589 --> 01:29:37,999
Untie.

688
01:29:43,696 --> 01:29:46,256
Now!

689
01:29:46,385 --> 01:29:49,345
Walk!

690
01:30:16,155 --> 01:30:18,485
Take this.

691
01:30:48,645 --> 01:30:53,397
Göktuğ, what are we going to do, brother?

692
01:30:53,397 --> 01:30:59,587
Osman Bey will do what's he going to do.
We need to get rid of those dogs.

693
01:30:59,669 --> 01:31:03,049
Let's go!
Come on!

694
01:31:30,531 --> 01:31:32,201
Let's go!

695
01:31:49,584 --> 01:31:56,244
Now, tell me everything from beginning
to the end, Osman Bey.

696
01:32:09,978 --> 01:32:16,898
You must be thankful to the Lord, Aygül.
This is a windfall for you.

697
01:32:18,263 --> 01:32:22,593
A person needs to go through
hard times to be wise.

698
01:32:23,148 --> 01:32:27,048
Alişar Bey supported us in our hard times.

699
01:32:27,404 --> 01:32:32,054
He came up like an angel from my Lord.

700
01:32:33,171 --> 01:32:38,741
He supported each one of us, you, me, and
your father.

701
01:32:39,565 --> 01:32:43,124
I appriciate him, but I am worried about
what's going to happen when...

702
01:32:43,124 --> 01:32:46,394
what happened in Kayı tribe is revealed,
Mother.

703
01:32:46,444 --> 01:32:49,974
This has been happening since my father
became the Bey.

704
01:32:50,747 --> 01:32:55,437
Look, Osman is on his way of Konya.
It seems like he will not return.

705
01:32:57,070 --> 01:33:01,840
The killer of my son.
Hell be with him!

706
01:33:01,843 --> 01:33:08,063
Right, but if something happens to Osman,
we all

707
01:33:08,527 --> 01:33:16,167
When it spreads to the nearest tribes,
I am not sure whose side they will take.

708
01:33:17,365 --> 01:33:21,855
Leave the nearest tribes aside,
Let it spread to the whole universe.

709
01:33:21,855 --> 01:33:28,172
So that everyone can see the end of
those who...

710
01:33:28,172 --> 01:33:32,842
stands against the tradition, rebels,
set their eyes to the throne.

711
01:33:32,842 --> 01:33:37,072
Also, the bannerlord is on our side.

712
01:33:37,207 --> 01:33:40,383
Aygül, be wise, my daughter.

713
01:33:40,383 --> 01:33:44,773
If you be a good wife to him,
not only you...

714
01:33:44,832 --> 01:33:48,102
but also your descendants will benefit
from this.

715
01:33:49,553 --> 01:33:51,313
Also...

716
01:33:52,117 --> 01:33:55,967
You are not worried about
Osman's situation, are you, Aygül?

717
01:33:56,021 --> 01:34:02,051
If I were to worry about him, we wouldn't
be here preparing to the wedding, mother.

718
01:34:02,796 --> 01:34:08,127
My only wish is to clear the Tribe from
Osman and his fellas and...

719
01:34:08,127 --> 01:34:11,637
see my father on the throne which
he deserves.

720
01:34:13,038 --> 01:34:15,230
You are right.

721
01:34:15,580 --> 01:34:19,460
You are right, my emerald-eyed daughter.

722
01:34:19,730 --> 01:34:21,920
You are right.

723
01:34:23,031 --> 01:34:30,991
We are in the right way, The ones who
are fake will vanish away, in sha Allah.

724
01:35:25,079 --> 01:35:29,099
Thank lord, we made it to this day,
my Sheik.

725
01:35:29,575 --> 01:35:38,505
After all those wars, we are building
our Khanqah (islamic lodge)

726
01:35:38,660 --> 01:35:41,910
Our booty is this.

727
01:35:42,171 --> 01:35:46,702
Booty, or entrustment, my Akça?

728
01:35:47,492 --> 01:35:52,332
Does victory come from us, or Allah?

729
01:36:00,837 --> 01:36:09,687
If they think as you think,
our situation is really bad.

730
01:36:37,882 --> 01:36:40,412
Spill it.

731
01:37:17,054 --> 01:37:22,234
- Summon the Yarens.
- Of course.

732
01:37:23,634 --> 01:37:28,074
Yarens, my Sheik summons you.

733
01:37:52,459 --> 01:37:59,879
In this mubarak Ramadan day,
you are working while fasting.

734
01:38:00,027 --> 01:38:05,277
I wanted you to take a breath.

735
01:38:09,163 --> 01:38:18,543
After emigration, Mecca polytheists
considered Muslims as a big threat.

736
01:38:18,766 --> 01:38:28,966
Especially, they think Damascus is under
threat.

737
01:38:29,120 --> 01:38:40,110
Because of that, they try to stop Muslims
before Muslims go stronger.

738
01:38:41,392 --> 01:38:48,142
The name of the spy they found in Medina
is İbn-i Selule.

739
01:38:49,062 --> 01:38:55,742
Don't forget, Yarens.
Time passes away.

740
01:38:55,858 --> 01:39:00,278
But, there is always an İbn-i Selule.

741
01:39:01,925 --> 01:39:10,698
At that time, Muslims learned that
Ebu Sufyan's caravan is....

742
01:39:10,698 --> 01:39:14,498
on the way of Damascus.

743
01:39:15,908 --> 01:39:21,208
Caravan, but what a caravan.

744
01:39:21,420 --> 01:39:26,290
There were about fifty thousand
dinar(currency) worth items.

745
01:39:29,617 --> 01:39:39,777
Ebu Sufyan realized that threat and
seek help from his friends from Mecca.

746
01:39:41,032 --> 01:39:48,372
A thousand people go to
protect the caravan.

747
01:39:48,659 --> 01:39:53,862
Our Efendi, who is the diamond of this
and the other world...

748
01:39:53,862 --> 01:39:56,295
May Allah send prayers and peace upon him

749
01:39:56,295 --> 01:40:00,482
He asks who to strike first...

750
01:40:00,482 --> 01:40:05,552
Caravan, or the army of polytheists?

751
01:40:09,197 --> 01:40:13,947
Most of them say caravan.

752
01:40:14,399 --> 01:40:21,689
But when our Prophet starts to tell
the truth by the light of revelations...

753
01:40:21,766 --> 01:40:24,766
... their thoughts change.

754
01:40:25,609 --> 01:40:30,234
They understand that
Allah's desire isn't on that.

755
01:40:30,234 --> 01:40:40,587
If they strike the caravan, they'll gain
an economical advantage and save the day.

756
01:40:40,587 --> 01:40:45,547
But if they strike
the army of polytheists...

757
01:40:46,101 --> 01:40:49,321
... their afterlives would be saved.

758
01:40:50,992 --> 01:40:55,842
Our holy Prophet...

759
01:40:55,842 --> 01:41:05,372
... wants the Muslims to save
humanity, not their day.

760
01:41:06,842 --> 01:41:15,342
My Allah, in the surah Anfal, tells us
that even booty is temporary.

761
01:41:15,964 --> 01:41:18,892
And says;

762
01:41:18,892 --> 01:41:22,379
In the name of God, the merciful and compassionate
[Surah Al-Anfal 8:1]

763
01:41:22,379 --> 01:41:29,545
The believers are only those who, when Allah
is mentioned, their hearts become fearful

764
01:41:29,545 --> 01:41:35,365
... and when His verses are recited to them...

765
01:41:35,365 --> 01:41:39,795
..it increases them in faith; and upon their Lord they rely
[Surah Al-Anfal 8:2]

766
01:41:40,794 --> 01:41:45,984
The ones who establish prayer,..

767
01:41:48,088 --> 01:41:54,618
...and from what We have provided them, they spend.
[Surah Al-Anfal 8:3]

768
01:41:57,258 --> 01:42:01,698
Those are the believers, truly.

769
01:42:04,752 --> 01:42:09,792
For them are degrees [of high position] with their Lord

770
01:42:10,347 --> 01:42:14,687
...and forgiveness and noble provision.
[Surah Al-Anfal 8:4]

771
01:42:16,654 --> 01:42:20,204
Long story short, friends...

772
01:42:20,585 --> 01:42:26,825
A Muslim's goal should be
to help humanity, not get booty.

773
01:42:28,123 --> 01:42:33,553
If not for the opportunities
Allah gave us...

774
01:42:33,581 --> 01:42:36,631
... we wouldn't have started
this Lodge's construction.

775
01:42:37,029 --> 01:42:42,269
So our success isn't from
our desires, it's from Allah.

776
01:42:44,832 --> 01:42:51,937
Our Prophet and his companion
emigrated to Medina...

777
01:42:51,937 --> 01:42:56,887
... to have the qualities
they believed in. But remember...

778
01:42:56,915 --> 01:43:00,325
... Muslims emigration didn't end.

779
01:43:02,512 --> 01:43:12,722
We'll continue emigrating to carry
the qualities to those who need them.

780
01:43:13,579 --> 01:43:18,289
This Lodge's purpose will be this.

781
01:43:18,782 --> 01:43:21,122
Hopefully.

782
01:43:33,340 --> 01:43:38,340
With Allah's commandment and
our Prophet's sunnah...

783
01:43:38,340 --> 01:43:42,273
... we're here to perform Aygül Hatun
and Alişar Bey's wedding.

784
01:43:42,273 --> 01:43:47,168
Aygül Hatun, daughter of Dündar. Do you
accept marrying Alişar, son of Mahmut...

785
01:43:47,168 --> 01:43:52,118
... with a dowry of
500 drams of gold?

786
01:43:52,274 --> 01:43:58,964
- Yes
- Do You?

787
01:44:00,123 --> 01:44:06,371
Alişar Bey, son of Mahmut. Do you accept
marrying Aygül Hatun, daughter of Dündar..

788
01:44:06,371 --> 01:44:10,042
... with the 500 gold you've
promised to give?

789
01:44:14,462 --> 01:44:23,497
- Yes.
- Do you?

790
01:44:23,497 --> 01:44:28,687
- Witnesses. Do you bear witness?
- Yes.

791
01:44:29,388 --> 01:44:32,718
By all the witnesses, I pronounce
you husband and wife...

792
01:44:32,924 --> 01:44:37,924
May my Rab bless your wedding, and keep
you together until the end of time. Amen.

793
01:45:07,977 --> 01:45:10,447
Father!

794
01:45:10,565 --> 01:45:12,965
Alişar Bey!

795
01:45:14,067 --> 01:45:17,247
What is going on?
What are you doing here?

796
01:45:17,418 --> 01:45:20,688
- What are you doing, Bahadır?
- Everything is ruined!

797
01:45:20,724 --> 01:45:26,954
They ambushed me and my Alps
in the forest! They killed all of them!

798
01:45:28,300 --> 01:45:33,580
What are we waiting for, Alişar Bey? Let's
go and drown them in their own blood!

799
01:45:34,113 --> 01:45:38,423
Now it's time to be a man!

800
01:45:44,859 --> 01:45:47,179
- Father!
- Father!

801
01:45:47,870 --> 01:45:50,720
- Dündar!
- Father!

802
01:45:59,665 --> 01:46:02,334
- Dündar!
- Father!

803
01:46:02,334 --> 01:46:05,704
- Dündar Bey!
- Father!

804
01:46:14,430 --> 01:46:17,930
Dündar!

805
01:46:19,113 --> 01:46:22,913
Father!

806
01:46:23,676 --> 01:46:27,136
Dündar!

807
01:46:37,045 --> 01:46:41,985
Take a look around with Böke. I have
somethings to talk to with Osman Bey.

808
01:46:58,599 --> 01:47:01,649
Start from the Monks of Margaret.

809
01:47:03,051 --> 01:47:07,881
Geyhatu was going to take
the Emperor down...

810
01:47:08,152 --> 01:47:11,092
... and put Sofia in his place.

811
01:47:11,154 --> 01:47:15,144
I've destroyed his attempt.

812
01:47:16,209 --> 01:47:20,659
You gave the traitor's
names to the Emperor.

813
01:47:21,374 --> 01:47:26,834
I took them from Böke's hands.
If you don't believe me, go ask him.

814
01:47:27,342 --> 01:47:30,102
Huh? Go!

815
01:47:31,822 --> 01:47:36,784
Monks of Margaret spies
are in the hands of the Emperor, right?

816
01:47:36,784 --> 01:47:40,217
I did what you couldn't do!

817
01:47:40,217 --> 01:47:47,667
Without one arrow, without
a drop of blood, I've defeated Geyhatu.

818
01:47:53,407 --> 01:47:56,043
Is that why Geyhatu is coming?

819
01:47:56,043 --> 01:48:00,183
I did what I could. I beat Geyhatu.

820
01:48:00,252 --> 01:48:05,412
Now it's your turn.
You'll find and destroy him.

821
01:48:06,622 --> 01:48:11,262
What about the information
you'll give me about Geyhatu?

822
01:48:11,498 --> 01:48:15,815
Boran will bring the laws.
Then you'll release me.

823
01:48:15,815 --> 01:48:19,065
Only then I will tell you.

824
01:48:19,762 --> 01:48:23,072
If Boran doesn't come...

825
01:48:24,432 --> 01:48:28,042
... I'll skin you alive.

826
01:48:28,269 --> 01:48:35,209
You'll witness your flesh being
separated from your bones.

827
01:49:07,735 --> 01:49:10,685
Pray to your religion, Osman.

828
01:49:11,196 --> 01:49:15,686
So that your Alps comes here at once.

829
01:49:21,426 --> 01:49:23,926
Tie him up.

830
01:49:40,244 --> 01:49:46,644
Die, for the love of Erlil Khan!

831
01:49:58,357 --> 01:50:03,557
Get him! Quick!

832
01:50:31,901 --> 01:50:34,429
Melik! What does the doctor say?

833
01:50:34,539 --> 01:50:39,709
He's excited, my Bey.
He'll be fine if he rests for a while.

834
01:50:41,620 --> 01:50:46,320
Dündar Bey is old blood.
He'll be fine.

835
01:50:46,494 --> 01:50:49,804
But there is no time to wait, Alişar Bey.

836
01:50:50,084 --> 01:50:52,194
A bloody payoff is awaiting us.

837
01:50:52,626 --> 01:50:58,586
If they want to spill blood, let's
finish the preparations, Bahadır.

838
01:51:04,046 --> 01:51:08,046
I'll cut the veins of this region...

839
01:51:09,034 --> 01:51:13,034
and they'll see how is it like
to play with us.

840
01:52:09,857 --> 01:52:11,097
Come, daughter.

841
01:52:16,306 --> 01:52:17,396
Bala.

842
01:52:18,740 --> 01:52:20,700
Let me do it, daughter.

843
01:52:20,721 --> 01:52:23,911
Helping my Sheikh is like a mission
for our Allah.

844
01:52:39,060 --> 01:52:42,620
- Thank you, Selcan Hatun.
- Thank you, my Sheikh.

845
01:52:45,412 --> 01:52:46,912
Welcome.

846
01:52:47,926 --> 01:52:49,436
Come.

847
01:53:06,244 --> 01:53:09,674
We were hoping to
get news from you.

848
01:53:10,090 --> 01:53:14,430
Bala said that the tent's
conditions are troubled.

849
01:53:17,246 --> 01:53:21,246
We didn't want to do anything without
Osman Bey's words.

850
01:53:21,796 --> 01:53:23,376
Bala daughter.

851
01:53:24,058 --> 01:53:28,838
Thank you. She stood by us. She
became a remedy to our grief.

852
01:53:29,319 --> 01:53:32,619
She helped us.

853
01:53:33,245 --> 01:53:37,245
But she couldn't resist...

854
01:53:37,545 --> 01:53:40,615
some things in the tent, my Sheikh.

855
01:53:41,277 --> 01:53:43,827
I know what Dündar Bey has done.

856
01:53:44,091 --> 01:53:48,091
But I don't know what Osman
Bey is doing now.

857
01:53:48,147 --> 01:53:49,507
My Osman...

858
01:53:50,302 --> 01:53:53,292
he was played.

859
01:53:53,349 --> 01:53:55,639
But he keeps fighting.

860
01:53:55,639 --> 01:53:58,579
He sets a trap to a trap.

861
01:53:58,793 --> 01:54:02,793
His intention is to show his uncle
what the truth is.

862
01:54:07,478 --> 01:54:10,158
That's why...

863
01:54:10,350 --> 01:54:13,890
he's objected Aygül's marriage.

864
01:54:16,626 --> 01:54:21,566
His intention is to solve
this problem with Aygül.

865
01:54:32,800 --> 01:54:33,520
Osman...

866
01:54:34,819 --> 01:54:40,639
always thought about his tent and
left his own good behind.

867
01:54:40,900 --> 01:54:44,600
He was sometimes mad, and
sometimes novice.

868
01:54:45,094 --> 01:54:48,804
However, he always did the
right thing because...

869
01:54:49,722 --> 01:54:52,852
his way was the right way.

870
01:54:54,028 --> 01:54:58,028
That's why he'll always
be tied to Allah...

871
01:54:58,573 --> 01:55:02,573
and he'll manage to get away...

872
01:55:03,188 --> 01:55:06,338
the bad situations around him, Inshaallah.

873
01:55:06,434 --> 01:55:08,314
Inshaallah, my Sheikh.

874
01:55:08,929 --> 01:55:10,549
Inshaallah.

875
01:55:15,112 --> 01:55:19,112
Thank you, my Sheikh. You
put my mind at rest.

876
01:55:19,204 --> 01:55:23,204
I wanted to relieve and now I'm relieved.

877
01:55:25,058 --> 01:55:29,058
- Keep praying for us.
- We're after the same purpose with not...

878
01:55:30,321 --> 01:55:33,841
only our prayers but also
our hearts, Selcan Hatun.

879
01:55:35,266 --> 01:55:39,266
We wish that the place that...

880
01:55:39,345 --> 01:55:43,725
will set up in this region
to be holy for Islam.

881
01:55:48,149 --> 01:55:49,409
Don't worry.

882
01:55:50,233 --> 01:55:54,233
Kayı tent is more crowded...

883
01:55:54,479 --> 01:55:56,919
than they think.

884
01:58:56,833 --> 01:59:00,113
We have an unfinished business, Osman.

885
01:59:00,776 --> 01:59:03,496
You're wrong, Böke.

886
01:59:03,875 --> 01:59:07,475
You'll find yourself in the judgment day.

887
02:01:12,817 --> 02:01:15,287
He can't go far away with an
arrow on his back.

888
02:01:16,777 --> 02:01:18,567
Find him.

889
02:01:46,258 --> 02:01:49,628
We were nourishing a serpent in our bosom.

890
02:01:51,485 --> 02:01:53,295
Too bad.

891
02:02:03,726 --> 02:02:05,126
My Bamsı Bey.

892
02:02:05,331 --> 02:02:09,331
- Are you okay?
- Thanks, my Konur. I'm fine.

893
02:02:09,467 --> 02:02:10,727
Thank you.

894
02:02:12,888 --> 02:02:17,778
How could they dare? I still can't
believe it, Bamsı Bey.

895
02:02:18,004 --> 02:02:19,874
I still can't believe it.

896
02:02:20,366 --> 02:02:22,126
Even Burçin...

897
02:02:23,267 --> 02:02:25,857
whom I see as my daughter...

898
02:02:26,812 --> 02:02:29,222
disobeyed us.

899
02:02:30,700 --> 02:02:35,500
This betrayal poisons everyone.

900
02:02:35,617 --> 02:02:38,087
Kulucahisar's feudal landlord...

901
02:02:38,377 --> 02:02:40,647
and the traitors among us.

902
02:02:41,382 --> 02:02:42,902
They're all the same.

903
02:02:45,415 --> 02:02:50,685
Unbelievers are our enemies. But
their hostility is clear.

904
02:02:50,852 --> 02:02:53,472
But the tratiors aren't like that.

905
02:02:54,164 --> 02:02:57,874
They seem like a friend and
they can hide hostility.

906
02:03:01,291 --> 02:03:05,291
Şahin and Demirci are
waiting for their execution.

907
02:03:07,583 --> 02:03:12,953
But the betrayal's pus keeps
suppurating, my Gündüz.

908
02:03:13,328 --> 02:03:18,028
Then it's time to squeeze
the pus, Bamsı Bey.

909
02:03:20,760 --> 02:03:21,990
Alps!

910
02:03:23,907 --> 02:03:28,237
Today is the day to qualify our weapons.

911
02:03:28,970 --> 02:03:33,940
Today is the day to
snub Alişar Bey.

912
02:03:34,906 --> 02:03:38,906
We'll go and strangle him in his place.

913
02:04:12,002 --> 02:04:15,352
Dündar Bey, you're doing wrong.

914
02:04:16,680 --> 02:04:18,370
You should rest.

915
02:04:18,381 --> 02:04:21,041
Dündar Bey, what are you doing?

916
02:04:24,766 --> 02:04:25,546
My Bey...

917
02:04:26,107 --> 02:04:27,357
Dündar Bey...

918
02:04:28,742 --> 02:04:33,222
Why are you up? Why are you in a hurry?

919
02:04:33,496 --> 02:04:36,526
You should rest.

920
02:04:36,571 --> 02:04:41,281
We tell him but he doesn't
understand, Zöhre Hatun.

921
02:04:41,926 --> 02:04:44,906
He keeps insisting to come.

922
02:04:45,304 --> 02:04:48,444
Alişar Bey should
send news to the Beys around.

923
02:04:48,494 --> 02:04:50,814
The tents should gather.

924
02:04:50,874 --> 02:04:54,944
- Let's see what they'll do.
- There's no time, Hatun.

925
02:04:55,008 --> 02:04:59,458
I should be with my Beys and horses.

926
02:04:59,957 --> 02:05:03,807
No one can say that I've escaped.

927
02:05:03,857 --> 02:05:06,077
There's no time.

928
02:05:06,154 --> 02:05:10,464
Your wounds haven't got better yet.
Don't.

929
02:05:11,023 --> 02:05:14,523
Even your shadow frightens people.

930
02:05:14,609 --> 02:05:18,229
Let Alişar Bey prepare.

931
02:05:18,692 --> 02:05:22,692
Then you'll hit the road. Then you'll take
our revenge.

932
02:05:24,031 --> 02:05:28,031
Get my horse ready now.

933
02:05:29,019 --> 02:05:32,619
Father, Zöhre Hatun is right.

934
02:05:32,671 --> 02:05:34,701
You should wait.

935
02:05:35,406 --> 02:05:39,036
I don't know anything about
laws and rights.

936
02:05:39,372 --> 02:05:42,732
They killed my child for this case.

937
02:05:43,470 --> 02:05:46,140
They can't kill my other child.

938
02:05:48,363 --> 02:05:53,223
I'll take my revenge and take the post
that I have a right to...

939
02:05:54,068 --> 02:05:58,068
and I'll kill the people who have...

940
02:05:58,257 --> 02:06:00,227
objected me.

941
02:07:02,634 --> 02:07:03,914
Brother.

942
02:07:04,943 --> 02:07:06,693
This is a bullet dhikr.

943
02:07:09,285 --> 02:07:11,245
He escaped.

944
02:07:24,080 --> 02:07:26,180
They shot him
while he was escaping.

945
02:07:27,865 --> 02:07:31,865
- Come on, Boran. Come on.
- Come on, brother.

946
02:09:16,781 --> 02:09:18,361
Alişar Bey!

947
02:09:24,485 --> 02:09:26,985
Open the door!

948
02:09:27,535 --> 02:09:31,215
- It's time to talk.
- Gündüz Bey!

949
02:09:31,341 --> 02:09:36,651
Let us. We'll break this door!

950
02:09:50,493 --> 02:09:52,133
You know.

951
02:09:52,253 --> 02:09:56,253
The door can't be locked
when the piker is inside.

952
02:09:57,177 --> 02:10:00,487
- Come on, Bamsı Bey!
- Ya Allah!

953
02:10:34,782 --> 02:10:36,402
Alişar!

954
02:10:38,526 --> 02:10:40,446
Alişar!

955
02:10:43,044 --> 02:10:44,714
Ya Allah!

956
02:10:58,189 --> 02:10:59,729
Alişar!

957
02:11:01,481 --> 02:11:03,501
Alişar!